[I] Limited Error Raster Compression

[T] LERC (Limited Error Raster Compression) is an open-source image and
[T] raster format from Esri which supports rapid encoding and decoding of
[T] any pixel type. The user sets the maximum compression error per pixel,
[T] and this C++ library encodes and decodes such images; it is used e.g. by
[T] GDAL and libtiff.

[U] https://github.com/esri/lerc

[A] Esri
[M] andrei32

[C] extra/tool
[F] CROSS

